 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 531765,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/2bc4d1072c570a54.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n(credit: modification of work by Belloy ME, Napolioni V, Greicius MD/<i>Neuron</i>)\n</figure>\n",
   "stem_html": "<p>The apolipoprotein E (APOE) gene is associated with Alzheimer's disease. This gene has three possible alleles, E2, E3 and E4. Recall that each person has two alleles for a gene. The graph shows Alzheimer risk of a person and the APOE allele combination they have.</p>\n<p>What can we conclude from this graph?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1039976,
     "content_html": "E4 allele increases likelihood of having Alzheimer's. E4/E4 combination has the most risk."
    },
    {
     "id": 1039977,
     "content_html": "E3 allele increases likelihood of having Alzheimer's. E3/E4 combination has the most risk."
    },
    {
     "id": 1039978,
     "content_html": "E2 allele increases likelihood of having Alzheimer's. E2/E3 combination has the most risk."
    },
    {
     "id": 1039979,
     "content_html": "People with different alleles for APOE have a higher risk for Alzheimer's."
    }
   ],
